/Title (Italy's water system relies on Alpine and Apennine basins, dominated by the Po River in the north and karst aquifers in the south. However, the country faces a critical transition as climate change intensifies droughts and aging infrastructure results in water losses exceeding 40%. To combat this, the efforts aim to transform obsolete pipelines into smart, resilient networks that can safely transport "blue gold" across the peninsula.)
